'' =============================================================================
''
''   File....... test-so109-conditional-brk-breaks.spin2
''   Purpose.... Decide prediction SO109 on SILICON: does a BRK whose condition
''               is false still enter the debug ISR, and which code does
''               GETBRK show for it
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 01 Oct 2026
''
'' =============================================================================

{ WHAT IS DECIDED (brief BRIEF-SO109, Parts 2 and 5)
    With "interrupt on BRK" armed in a cog's debug ISR, a BRK in that cog's
    program does two things: it raises the debug interrupt, and it records
    its 8-bit operand as the break code that GETBRK D WCZ returns in
    D[31:24] inside the ISR.
    Prediction under test (an independent reading of the logic, never
    observed on a part by its authors): the interrupt half ignores the
    BRK's flag condition, the code half honours it. So a condition-FALSE
    BRK still enters the ISR (discriminator A), and GETBRK then shows the
    code of the last condition-TRUE BRK this cog ran - a STALE code - not
    the false BRK's own operand (discriminator B). A BRK cancelled by SKIP,
    or sitting behind a taken branch, is cancelled on both halves.

  WHAT PARALLAX SAYS (documentary sources; read before writing the outcomes)
    Spin2 v55 change notes (spin2-v55-text.txt:61-64):
      "PASM DEBUG instructions can be now preceded by a condition, not just
       a _RET_."
      "Because the BRK instruction used for DEBUG is handled early in the
       pipeline, a condition has no effect, though an _RET_ will execute
       normally."
      "In order to make the BRK instruction conditional, an
       opposite-condition SKIP instruction is placed before it, causing the
       BRK to execute on the desired condition."
    P2 Documentation v35, DEBUG INTERRUPT > BRK (silicon-doc-text.txt:2491):
      "Regardless of the execution condition, the BRK instruction will
       trigger a debug interrupt, if enabled. The execution condition only
       gates the writing of the 8-bit code"
    Discriminator A: the study, v55 :62 and P2 Documentation :2491 ALL say
      a condition-false BRK enters the ISR. "Not entered" refutes all three.
    Discriminator B: the study and P2 Documentation :2491 say STALE (the
      condition gates the code write). v55 :62 read literally ("a condition
      has no effect") says OWN (the false BRK latches its own code). The
      program prints which reading the bench matched.
    Sites w3 and w4 (if_z SKIP #1 ahead of an unconditional BRK) are the
      very workaround v55 :63-64 documents, and the shape pnut-ts 1.55.8
      emits for "if_c debug(...)".

  RIG
    Any P2 board, NOTHING attached. No bench pin is touched. Pin P62 (the
    host serial TX line) carries the report as plain async serial, 8-N-1,
    2,000,000 baud, from a P_ASYNC_TX smart pin run by cog 0. P63 is not
    touched. Compile WITHOUT -d: there is NO DEBUG in this program, because
    the construction itself owns everything PNut's debugger would own -
    the HUBSET debug-enable/write-protect word, the per-cog debug hub
    areas, and the debug interrupt. A -d build would collide with it.
    Cog 0 (Spin2) is the starter and the reporter. Cog 1 is the target and
    runs nothing else. No other cog is started.

  CONSTRUCTION (cog 0, in this order)
    1. Mailbox at MBOX = $7_0000 (hub RAM, below the top 16 KB at $7C000):
         MBOX+0  next-record pointer, set to MBOX+8
         MBOX+4  done flag, cleared (the target writes 1 as its last act)
         MBOX+8  records: record k at MBOX+8+8k = GETBRK word, then the
                 $1FF (IRET0) word; capacity REC_CAP = 32 records. At most
                 14 can occur (the COGINIT entry + 13 BRK sites, all
                 straight-line), so the ISR (which has no bound check)
                 cannot run past MBOX_END = $7_0108.
       Non-overlap is checked at run time (control W): the program image
       ends below MBOX, and cog 0's stack (address of a local of main())
       lies at least STACK_MARGIN = $1_0000 bytes below MBOX. This build:
       see VERIFIED OPCODES below for the image size.
    2. HUBSET ##$2000_0002 (inline PASM). P2 Documentation :2747-2761:
       D = %0010_xxxx_xxxx_xxLW_DDDD_DDDD_DDDD_DDDD; L = 0 (no lock),
       W = 0 (top 16 KB writable at both its ranges), D[15:0] = %10 (debug
       interrupt enabled for cog 1 only). It also clears every other cog's
       enable and write protection. If the boot left the lock set, this
       write is ignored: the read-back (3) or the positive controls catch it.
    3. Copy the 16-long ISR image to cog 1's ISR-image ("load") area and
       read it back. P2 Documentation :2429 and table 25 (:2446-2477): the
       image loads from $FF840 + (!cog << 7); cog 1 -> $FF840 + ($E << 7)
       = $FFF40..$FFF7F; registers $000..$00F save to $FFF00..$FFF3F.
       Read-back must match all 16 longs (gate G0). The same 16 longs read
       at $7FF40 (the normal-range alias of the top 16 KB with W = 0,
       P2 Documentation :2754-2755, :2870) are printed, informational only.
    4. COGINIT cog 1, cog exec, from the target image (PTRB = its hub
       address). The debug-enabled cog takes its first debug interrupt on
       that COGINIT (P2 Documentation :2397); the ISR arms "interrupt on
       BRK" (BRK #$10 inside the ISR: bit %E only, :2508, :2517) on every
       entry, and exits through the ROM at $1FD (:2435-2439).
    5. Wait up to 1 s for the done flag; then COGSTOP cog 1, HUBSET
       ##$2000_0000 (debug enables all off), and report whatever records
       exist (a timeout still prints them).

  THE ISR IMAGE (exactly 16 longs, org 0; one 8-byte record per entry)
    getbrk isr_t wcz   [31:24] = break code, [23] = 1 on the COGINIT entry
    mov isr_r, $1FF    IRET0: return address [19:0], saved C [31], Z [30]
    rdlong/wrlong x4   append (isr_t, isr_r) at long[MBOX], advance it by 8
    brk #$10           re-arm interrupt-on-BRK only (no single step)
    jmp #\$1FD         ROM exit: restore $000..$00F, RETI0

  THE TARGET IMAGE (cog 1, org 0) - BRK SITES, cog addresses from THIS
  listing (pnut-ts 1.55.8). Each test BRK is followed by two NOPs; a
  record is attributed to a site when its return address is the BRK's
  address + 1 or + 2.
    site  BRK   code  shape                        flags at the BRK
    p1    $002  $A1   brk (positive control)       (not judged)
    e1    $006  $B2   if_z  brk   -- FALSE         C=0 Z=0 (mov y,#1 wcz)
    t1    $00A  $C3   if_nz brk   -- true          C=0 Z=0
    t2    $00E  $D4   if_z  brk   -- true          C=0 Z=1 (mov y,#0 wcz)
    e2    $012  $E5   if_nz brk   -- FALSE         C=0 Z=1
    e3    $016  $96   if_c  brk   -- FALSE (C)     C=0 Z=1
    s1    $01A  $F1   skip #1 / brk                C=0 Z=1 (carried)
    j1    $01E  $F2   jmp over / brk               C=0 Z=1 (carried)
    w1    $023  $F3   if_z jmp over / brk, Z=1     C=0 Z=1  (unwanted)
    w2    $028  $F4   if_z jmp over / brk, Z=0     C=0 Z=0  (wanted)
    w3    $02D  $F5   if_z skip #1 / brk, Z=1      C=0 Z=1  (unwanted)
    w4    $032  $F6   if_z skip #1 / brk, Z=0      C=0 Z=0  (wanted)
    p2    $035  $A9   brk (closing positive ctl)   C=0 Z=0
    The table is also CON constants (BRK_xx); control W re-derives every
    address from the image's labels and fails the run if any differs.

  PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (fixed before the run; the program prints them)
    STUDY PREDICTION - exactly 10 records, in this order:
      #  site   code         return     saved flags
      0  entry  any, b23=1   $000       -
      1  p1     $A1          $003/$004  -
      2  e1     $A1 (stale)  $007/$008  C0 Z0
      3  t1     $C3          $00B/$00C  C0 Z0
      4  t2     $D4          $00F/$010  C0 Z1
      5  e2     $D4 (stale)  $013/$014  C0 Z1
      6  e3     $D4 (stale)  $017/$018  C0 Z1
      7  w2     $F4          $029/$02A  C0 Z0
      8  w4     $F6          $033/$034  C0 Z0
      9  p2     $A9          $036/$037  C0 Z0
      No record from s1, j1, w1 or w3.
    CONDITION HONOURED: 7 records (entry, p1, t1, t2, w2, w4, p2); nothing
      from e1, e2, e3, while t1 and t2 entered.
                                      -> VERDICT SO109 BREAK: REFUTED
      (nothing from e1-e3 AND no t1 or t2 record -> INCONCLUSIVE: conditional
      BRKs not breaking at all is not the same finding)
    LATCH IGNORES THE CONDITION TOO: e1/e2/e3 records carry $B2/$E5/$96.
                                      -> VERDICT SO109 CODE: REFUTED (OWN)
    CANCEL FAILED: any record from s1, j1, w1 or w3.
                                      -> VERDICT SO109 CANCELS: REFUTED
    IDIOM SUPPRESSED A WANTED BREAK: no w2 or no w4 record (or a wrong code).
                                      -> VERDICT SO109 IDIOMS: REFUTED
    SAVED FLAG CONTRADICTS ITS SITE: a record's $1FF C/Z differ from the
      flags its site set (table above; p1 not judged). That record says
      nothing about a false condition -> that verdict INCONCLUSIVE.
    ATTRIBUTION UNCERTAIN: any record after record 0 whose return address
      is outside every site window -> all four verdicts INCONCLUSIVE (the
      count and codes are still printed).
    Anything else: INCONCLUSIVE, unpredicted pattern, named on the line.

  GATES (setup check + positive controls; any failure prints RIG FAIL and
  "NO VERDICT SO109", never a verdict - the run is inconclusive, not a
  refutation)
    W  : construction - ISR image is 16 longs; every BRK site address
         derived from the labels equals the listing table; the ISR's
         mailbox long equals MBOX; MBOX region below $7C000; image and
         stack below MBOX.
    G0 : load-area read-back matched (16 of 16).
    G1 : at least one record; the record pointer is aligned and in range.
    G2 : record 0 has GETBRK bit 23 set (its code and return address are
         printed, not judged - the code is whatever cog 1 last latched since
         reset; the address is expected to be $000, an inference no verdict
         rests on).
    G3 : a p1 record: code $A1, bit 23 clear.
    G4 : a p2 record: code $A9, bit 23 clear.
    G5 : done flag set within 1 s.

  VERDICT LINES (names fixed)
    VERDICT SO109 BREAK:   did e1, e2, e3 enter the ISR (discriminator A)
    VERDICT SO109 CODE:    STALE (study, P2 Documentation :2491) / OWN
                           (v55 :62 read literally) / OTHER (discr. B);
                           needs the BREAK result and the t1/t2 controls
    VERDICT SO109 CANCELS: no record from s1, j1, w1, w3
    VERDICT SO109 IDIOMS:  w2 (JMP idiom) and w4 (SKIP idiom) deliver
                           their own codes $F4 / $F6

  DEPENDS ON CLAIMS THE BRIEF MARKS INFERRED OR UNDETERMINED
    - where the entry after a BRK lands: attribution accepts +1 or +2; an
      address outside both makes the verdicts INCONCLUSIVE, not wrong.
    - that the COGINIT entry falls on the first instruction: record 0 is
      identified by b23 alone (first entry since COGINIT); its return
      address is printed and compared with $000 for information only, since
      no verdict depends on it (adopted from the pre-run review).
    - what the boot leaves in the lock / write protect / enables: G0 and
      the positive controls catch a lock left set.
    - record 0's code: printed, never judged.
    - the $7FF40 alias of the load area: the brief marks it inferred;
      P2 Documentation :2754-2755 states it. Printed, not gated.

  VERIFIED OPCODES (pnut-ts -l v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, NO -d; read from the
  .lst hub image; object offsets, cog addresses in brackets)
    Image: OBJ 9,768 bytes + VAR 248 bytes; .bin 16,048 bytes (with the
      interpreter), so the program ends far below MBOX = $7_0000.
    CON: HUBSET_BRK_COG1 = $2000_0002, LOAD_AREA = $000F_FF40,
      SAVE_AREA = $000F_FF00, LOAD_ALIAS = $0007_FF40, MBOX_END = $0007_0108,
      TX_X = $0064_0007 (100 clocks per bit, 8 bits).
    ISR image $0B0..$0EF = 16 longs [$000..$00F] (isr_end = $0F0 [$010]):
      $0B0 [$000] getbrk isr_t wcz     $FD781435  D=$00A, C=Z=1
      $0B4 [$001] mov isr_r, $1FF      $F60017FF  D=$00B, S=$1FF
      $0B8 [$002] rdlong isr_p, isr_b  $FB00180D
      $0BC [$003] wrlong isr_t, isr_p  $FC60140C
      $0C0 [$004] add isr_p, #4        $F1041804   ($0C8 [$006] the same)
      $0C4 [$005] wrlong isr_r, isr_p  $FC60160C
      $0CC [$007] wrlong isr_p, isr_b  $FC60180D
      $0D0 [$008] brk #$10             $FD642036  D=$010 (%E only)
      $0D4 [$009] jmp #\$1FD           $FD8001FD  bit 20 (R) = 0: absolute
      $0D8..$0E0 [$00A..$00C] isr_t, isr_r, isr_p = 0
      $0E4 [$00D] isr_b = $0007_0000 (MBOX); $0E8, $0EC pad = 0
    Target image from $0F0 [$000]; tgt_y at $1E0 [$03C]:
      mov tgt_y,#1 wcz  $F61C7801     mov tgt_y,#0 wcz  $F61C7800
      $0F8 [$002] p1  brk #$A1         $FD654236  cond 1111
      $108 [$006] e1  if_z brk #$B2    $AD656436  cond 1010
      $118 [$00A] t1  if_nz brk #$C3   $5D658636  cond 0101
      $128 [$00E] t2  if_z brk #$D4    $AD65A836  cond 1010
      $138 [$012] e2  if_nz brk #$E5   $5D65CA36  cond 0101
      $148 [$016] e3  if_c brk #$96    $CD652C36  cond 1100
      $154 [$019] s1  skip #1          $FD640231
      $158 [$01A]     brk #$F1         $FD65E236
      $164 [$01D] j1  jmp #j1_land     $FD900004  relative, +1
      $168 [$01E]     brk #$F2         $FD65E436
      $178 [$022] w1  if_z jmp #w1_land $AD900004
      $17C [$023]     brk #$F3         $FD65E636
      $18C [$027] w2  if_z jmp #w2_land $AD900004
      $190 [$028]     brk #$F4         $FD65E836
      $1A0 [$02C] w3  if_z skip #1     $AD640231
      $1A4 [$02D]     brk #$F5         $FD65EA36
      $1B4 [$031] w4  if_z skip #1     $AD640231
      $1B8 [$032]     brk #$F6         $FD65EC36
      $1C4 [$035] p2  brk #$A9         $FD655236
      $1D0 [$038] mov tgt_y, #1        $F6047801
      $1D4 [$039] augs                 $FF000380  ($0007_0004 >> 9)
      $1D8 [$03A] wrlong tgt_y, #$004  $FC647804  = ##MBOX_DONE
      $1DC [$03B] jmp #$               $FD9FFFFC
    Inline PASM (bytecode stream, unaligned):
      brk_enable_cog1  $4FF: $FF900000 (AUGD) + $FD640400 = hubset ##$2000_0002
      brk_disable_all  $513: $FF900000 (AUGD) + $FD640000 = hubset ##$2000_0000

  HOW TO RUN
    Compile: pnut-ts test-so109-conditional-brk-breaks.spin2     (NO -d)
    Load to RAM WITH RESET and listen at 2,000,000 baud, e.g.
      pnut-term-ts -r test-so109-conditional-brk-breaks.bin -b 2000000
      (headless: add --headless --end-marker)
    Cog 0 waits STARTUP_MS = 1 s before the first byte, then prints about
    90 lines in well under a second. Done when you see the four
    "VERDICT SO109 ..." lines (or "NO VERDICT SO109"), then "=== END ==="
    and DEBUG_END_SESSION (sent as plain text).
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq          = 200_000_000

  TX_PIN            = 62                ' host serial TX (the report link); no bench pin used
  BAUD              = 2_000_000
  TX_BIT_CLOCKS     = _clkfreq / BAUD   ' 100 clocks per bit
  TX_MODE           = P_ASYNC_TX | P_OE
  TX_X              = (TX_BIT_CLOCKS << 16) | 7     ' X[31:16] clocks/bit, X[4:0] = 8 bits - 1
  TX_BUSY_BIT       = $8000_0000        ' RQPIN() Zval[31] = C = 'busy' (v55 :544; P2 Doc :4707)
  STARTUP_MS        = 1000              ' let the host settle on the line before the first byte

  TARGET_COG        = 1
  DONE_TIMEOUT_MS   = 1000
  DONE_VALUE        = 1                 ' the target writes this to MBOX_DONE last

CON ' ---- Debug Interrupt Plumbing (P2 Documentation :2427-2477, :2747-2761) ----
  HUBSET_BRK_COG1   = $2000_0000 | (1 << TARGET_COG)        ' $2000_0002: L=0, W=0, cog 1 only
  HUBSET_BRK_NONE   = $2000_0000                            ' L=0, W=0, no cog enabled
  SAVE_AREA         = $F_F800 + ((!TARGET_COG & $F) << 7)   ' $FFF00, registers $000..$00F saved
  LOAD_AREA         = $F_F840 + ((!TARGET_COG & $F) << 7)   ' $FFF40, ISR image loaded from here
  LOAD_ALIAS        = LOAD_AREA - $8_0000                   ' $7FF40, normal-range alias (W=0)
  ISR_LONGS         = 16
  HUB_TOP16K        = $7_C000           ' last 16 KB of hub RAM (aliased at $FC000..$FFFFF)

CON ' ---- Mailbox ----
  MBOX              = $7_0000
  MBOX_NEXT         = MBOX              ' next-record pointer
  MBOX_DONE         = MBOX + 4          ' done flag
  MBOX_REC          = MBOX + 8          ' record k at MBOX_REC + 8k: GETBRK word, $1FF word
  REC_CAP           = 32                ' at most 14 records can occur
  MBOX_END          = MBOX_REC + REC_CAP * 8
  STACK_MARGIN      = $1_0000           ' cog 0's stack must sit this far below MBOX

  GETBRK_B23        = $0080_0000        ' GETBRK WCZ bit 23: COGINIT entry
  RET_MASK          = $000F_FFFF        ' IRET0 [19:0] return address

CON ' ---- BRK Sites (cog addresses from the pnut-ts 1.55.8 listing) ----
  #0, S_P1, S_E1, S_T1, S_T2, S_E2, S_E3, S_S1, S_J1, S_W1, S_W2, S_W3, S_W4, S_P2, SITE_COUNT
  S_ENTRY           = -1                ' the COGINIT entry (record 0)
  S_NONE            = -2                ' return address outside every site window

  BRK_P1            = $002
  BRK_E1            = $006
  BRK_T1            = $00A
  BRK_T2            = $00E
  BRK_E2            = $012
  BRK_E3            = $016
  BRK_S1            = $01A
  BRK_J1            = $01E
  BRK_W1            = $023
  BRK_W2            = $028
  BRK_W3            = $02D
  BRK_W4            = $032
  BRK_P2            = $035

  ' site kinds
  #0, K_POS, K_FALSE, K_TRUE, K_CANCEL, K_IDIOM

  ' saved flags in the $1FF word, as (C << 1) | Z  (C = bit 31, Z = bit 30)
  FLAGS_ANY         = -1
  FLAGS_C0Z0        = %00
  FLAGS_C0Z1        = %01

  ' expected-record tables
  #0, TBL_STUDY, TBL_ABSENT, TBL_OWN
  CODE_ANY          = -1

VAR ' ---- Analysis State ----
  long recCount                         ' records read from the mailbox
  long recSite[REC_CAP]                 ' attributed site of each record
  long siteHits[SITE_COUNT]             ' records attributed to each site
  long siteRec[SITE_COUNT]              ' first record index at each site
  long failCount                        ' gating failures
  long unattributed                     ' records (after record 0) outside every site window


PUB main() | stackProbe, startTick, bDone
'' Run the SO109 rig: check the construction, arm cog 1's debug interrupt,
'' load the ISR image, start the target, wait for done, then report.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local stackProbe - its address marks cog 0's stack (control W)
' @local startTick - CT when the wait for the done flag began
' @local bDone - TRUE when the target set the done flag in time

  pinstart(TX_PIN, TX_MODE, TX_X, 0)
  waitms(STARTUP_MS)
  failCount := 0
  say(string("=== SO109: does a condition-false BRK enter the debug ISR, and which code does GETBRK show? ==="))
  say(string("no DEBUG build: plain serial on P62, 2000000 baud 8-N-1; target = cog 1; no bench pin used"))
  print_predictions()
  put_nl()
  say(string("--- CONTROL W: construction ---"))
  check_construction(@stackProbe)
  if failCount <> 0
    say(string("NO VERDICT SO109 - a construction control failed (RIG FAIL above); cog 1 was not started"))
    finish()

  long[MBOX_NEXT] := MBOX_REC
  long[MBOX_DONE] := 0
  longfill(MBOX_REC, 0, REC_CAP * 2)
  brk_enable_cog1()
  put_nl()
  say(string("--- GATE G0: ISR image -> cog 1 load area $FFF40, read back ---"))
  if load_isr() <> 0
    brk_disable_all()
    say(string("RIG FAIL: G0 load area not written (lock left set, or write protection still on)"))
    say(string("NO VERDICT SO109 - setup failed; the run is INCONCLUSIVE, not a refutation; cog 1 was not started"))
    finish()

  coginit(TARGET_COG, @tgt, 0)
  startTick := getct()
  repeat until long[MBOX_DONE] == DONE_VALUE or getct() - startTick > clkfreq / 1000 * DONE_TIMEOUT_MS
  bDone := long[MBOX_DONE] == DONE_VALUE
  cogstop(TARGET_COG)
  brk_disable_all()
  report(bDone)
  finish()


PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends a run when DEBUG_END_SESSION
' appears in its output (--end-marker / --exit-on-end-session); here it is plain text.
'

  say(string("=== END ==="))
  say(string("DEBUG_END_SESSION"))
  repeat


PRI brk_enable_cog1()
' HUBSET %0010 form: lock clear, write protection clear, debug interrupt for cog 1 only.
'

  org
                hubset  ##HUBSET_BRK_COG1
  end


PRI brk_disable_all()
' HUBSET %0010 form: lock clear, write protection clear, no cog debug-enabled.
'

  org
                hubset  ##HUBSET_BRK_NONE
  end


PRI print_predictions() | tblIdx, siteIdx
' Print the outcomes fixed before the run, generated from the same tables
' the verdicts use.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local tblIdx - row of the study table
' @local siteIdx - site of that row

  say(string("PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (fixed before the run):"))
  say(string("  study prediction: exactly 10 records, in this order; no record from s1, j1, w1, w3"))
  say(string("   #  site   BRK   code          return      saved flags"))
  repeat tblIdx from 0 to table_len(TBL_STUDY) - 1
    siteIdx := exp_site(TBL_STUDY, tblIdx)
    put_str(string("   "))
    put_dec(tblIdx)
    put_str(string("  "))
    put_str(site_name(siteIdx))
    if siteIdx == S_ENTRY
      say(string("  -     any, b23=1    $000        -"))
    else
      put_str(string("  $"))
      put_hex(site_brk(siteIdx), 3)
      put_str(string("  $"))
      put_hex(exp_code(TBL_STUDY, tblIdx), 2)
      if site_kind(siteIdx) == K_FALSE
        put_str(string(" (stale)"))
      else
        put_str(string("        "))
      put_str(string("  $"))
      put_hex(site_brk(siteIdx) + 1, 3)
      put_str(string("/$"))
      put_hex(site_brk(siteIdx) + 2, 3)
      put_str(string("   "))
      put_flags_expect(site_flags(siteIdx))
      put_nl()
  say(string("  BREAK  : e1/e2/e3 enter the ISR -> CONFIRMED (study; v55 :62 and P2 Documentation :2491 agree)"))
  say(string("           none of e1/e2/e3 enters, t1 and t2 do (7 records) -> REFUTED, condition honoured"))
  say(string("  CODE   : e1/e2/e3 show $A1/$D4/$D4 = STALE  -> CONFIRMED (study; P2 Documentation :2491)"))
  say(string("           e1/e2/e3 show $B2/$E5/$96 = OWN    -> REFUTED (latch ignores the condition; v55 :62 literal)"))
  say(string("  CANCELS: no record from s1, j1, w1, w3       -> CONFIRMED; any record there -> REFUTED"))
  say(string("  IDIOMS : w2 shows $F4 and w4 shows $F6       -> CONFIRMED; missing or wrong code -> REFUTED"))
  say(string("  saved C/Z contradicting a site, or a record outside every site window -> INCONCLUSIVE"))
  say(string("  gates (else RIG FAIL / NO VERDICT): read-back 16/16; >=1 record; record 0 b23=1 (ret printed only);"))
  say(string("         p1 record $A1 b23=0; p2 record $A9 b23=0; done flag within 1 s"))


PRI put_flags_expect(flagRule)
' Print an expected-flags cell.
'
' @param flagRule - FLAGS_ANY or (C << 1) | Z

  if flagRule == FLAGS_ANY
    put_str(string("-"))
  else
    put_str(string("C"))
    put_dec((flagRule >> 1) & 1)
    put_str(string(" Z"))
    put_dec(flagRule & 1)


PRI check_construction(pStack) | siteIdx, derived, imageEnd
' Control W: image shape, site table, mailbox placement.
'
' @param pStack - address of a local of main() (cog 0's stack)

' Local Variables:
' @local siteIdx - site being checked
' @local derived - site BRK address derived from the image labels
' @local imageEnd - hub address just past the target image

  put_str(string("  ISR image: $"))
  put_hex(@isr, 5)
  put_str(string("..$"))
  put_hex(@isr_end - 1, 5)
  put_str(string(" = "))
  put_dec((@isr_end - @isr) / 4)
  say(string(" longs (must be 16)"))
  if @isr_end - @isr <> ISR_LONGS * 4
    say(string("RIG FAIL: W ISR image is not 16 longs"))
    failCount++
  put_str(string("  ISR mailbox long = $"))
  put_hex(isr_b, 5)
  put_str(string(" (must be MBOX $"))
  put_hex(MBOX, 5)
  say(string(")"))
  if isr_b <> MBOX
    say(string("RIG FAIL: W ISR mailbox long differs from MBOX"))
    failCount++
  repeat siteIdx from 0 to SITE_COUNT - 1
    derived := site_label_addr(siteIdx)
    if derived <> site_brk(siteIdx)
      put_str(string("RIG FAIL: W site "))
      put_str(site_name(siteIdx))
      put_str(string(" BRK at $"))
      put_hex(derived, 3)
      put_str(string(" in the image, table says $"))
      put_hex(site_brk(siteIdx), 3)
      put_nl()
      failCount++
  say(string("  site BRK addresses: derived from the image labels, compared with the listing table"))
  imageEnd := @tgt_end
  put_str(string("  target image: $"))
  put_hex(@tgt, 5)
  put_str(string("..$"))
  put_hex(imageEnd - 1, 5)
  put_str(string("   cog 0 stack near $"))
  put_hex(pStack, 5)
  put_str(string("   mailbox $"))
  put_hex(MBOX, 5)
  put_str(string("..$"))
  put_hex(MBOX_END - 1, 5)
  put_str(string("   top 16 KB from $"))
  put_hex(HUB_TOP16K, 5)
  put_nl()
  if MBOX_END > HUB_TOP16K
    say(string("RIG FAIL: W mailbox reaches into the top 16 KB"))
    failCount++
  if imageEnd >= MBOX or pStack + STACK_MARGIN > MBOX
    say(string("RIG FAIL: W program image or cog 0 stack is not clear below the mailbox"))
    failCount++
  put_str(string("  load area $"))
  put_hex(LOAD_AREA, 5)
  put_str(string(" (alias $"))
  put_hex(LOAD_ALIAS, 5)
  put_str(string("), save area $"))
  put_hex(SAVE_AREA, 5)
  put_str(string("; HUBSET $"))
  put_hex(HUBSET_BRK_COG1, 8)
  put_nl()
  if failCount == 0
    say(string("  control W: all passed"))


PRI load_isr() : mismatches | longIdx, imageLong, backLong, aliasLong, aliasDiffs
' Gate G0: copy the ISR image to cog 1's load area, read it back, compare.
'
' @returns mismatches - load-area longs that differ from the image

' Local Variables:
' @local longIdx - long being compared
' @local imageLong - the image long
' @local backLong - the long read back at the load area
' @local aliasLong - the long read at the normal-range alias
' @local aliasDiffs - alias longs that differ (informational)

  longmove(LOAD_AREA, @isr, ISR_LONGS)
  mismatches := 0
  aliasDiffs := 0
  repeat longIdx from 0 to ISR_LONGS - 1
    imageLong := long[@isr][longIdx]
    backLong := long[LOAD_AREA][longIdx]
    aliasLong := long[LOAD_ALIAS][longIdx]
    put_str(string("  +"))
    put_dec(longIdx)
    put_str(string("  image $"))
    put_hex(imageLong, 8)
    put_str(string("  read back $"))
    put_hex(backLong, 8)
    put_str(string("  alias $"))
    put_hex(aliasLong, 8)
    if backLong <> imageLong
      mismatches++
      put_str(string("  MISMATCH"))
    if aliasLong <> imageLong
      aliasDiffs++
    put_nl()
  put_str(string("  G0 read-back matched "))
  put_dec(ISR_LONGS - mismatches)
  put_str(string(" of 16; alias $7FF40 matched "))
  put_dec(ISR_LONGS - aliasDiffs)
  say(string(" of 16 (alias informational)"))


PRI report(bDone) | rawNext, recIdx, siteIdx
' Read the mailbox, print every record, run the gates, then the verdicts.
'
' @param bDone - TRUE when the done flag was set in time

' Local Variables:
' @local rawNext - the next-record pointer as the ISR left it
' @local recIdx - record being processed
' @local siteIdx - site being cleared

  put_nl()
  say(string("--- RECORDS (raw GETBRK word, raw $1FF word, decoded, attributed site) ---"))
  rawNext := long[MBOX_NEXT]
  put_str(string("  next-record pointer $"))
  put_hex(rawNext, 5)
  put_str(string("  done flag "))
  put_dec(long[MBOX_DONE])
  put_nl()
  recCount := 0
  if rawNext < MBOX_REC or rawNext > MBOX_END or ((rawNext - MBOX_REC) & 7) <> 0
    say(string("RIG FAIL: G1 next-record pointer out of range or misaligned; records not read"))
    failCount++
  else
    recCount := (rawNext - MBOX_REC) / 8
  repeat siteIdx from 0 to SITE_COUNT - 1
    siteHits[siteIdx] := 0
    siteRec[siteIdx] := -1
  unattributed := 0
  if recCount > 0
    repeat recIdx from 0 to recCount - 1
      recSite[recIdx] := attribute(recIdx)
      siteIdx := recSite[recIdx]
      if siteIdx >= 0
        if siteHits[siteIdx] == 0
          siteRec[siteIdx] := recIdx
        siteHits[siteIdx]++
      elseif siteIdx == S_NONE
        unattributed++
      print_record(recIdx)
  put_str(string("  record count "))
  put_dec(recCount)
  put_str(string("; unattributed "))
  put_dec(unattributed)
  put_nl()
  put_nl()
  say(string("--- GATES G1..G5: setup check and positive controls ---"))
  check_gates(bDone)
  put_nl()
  if failCount <> 0
    say(string("NO VERDICT SO109 - setup failed (RIG FAIL above); the run is INCONCLUSIVE, not a refutation"))
  else
    say(string("--- OUTCOME CHECKS (whole-run patterns; informational) ---"))
    print_table_check(TBL_STUDY, string("  10-record study prediction (stale codes)  : "))
    print_table_check(TBL_ABSENT, string("  7-record erratum-absent pattern           : "))
    print_table_check(TBL_OWN, string("  10-record latch-ignores-condition (OWN)   : "))
    put_nl()
    verdict_break()
    verdict_code()
    verdict_cancels()
    verdict_idioms()


PRI attribute(recIdx) : siteIdx | retAddr, scanIdx
' Attribute one record to a site by its return address.
'
' @param recIdx - record index
' @returns siteIdx - S_P1..S_P2, S_ENTRY (record 0 at $000), or S_NONE

' Local Variables:
' @local retAddr - the record's return address
' @local scanIdx - site being tried

  retAddr := rec_ret(recIdx)
  siteIdx := S_NONE
  if recIdx == 0 and rec_b23(0) == 1
    siteIdx := S_ENTRY
  else
    repeat scanIdx from 0 to SITE_COUNT - 1
      if retAddr == site_brk(scanIdx) + 1 or retAddr == site_brk(scanIdx) + 2
        siteIdx := scanIdx
        quit


PRI print_record(recIdx) | siteIdx
' Print one record raw and decoded.
'
' @param recIdx - record index

' Local Variables:
' @local siteIdx - the record's attributed site

  siteIdx := recSite[recIdx]
  put_str(string("  rec "))
  put_dec2(recIdx)
  put_str(string("  GETBRK $"))
  put_hex(rec_brk(recIdx), 8)
  put_str(string("  $1FF $"))
  put_hex(rec_iret(recIdx), 8)
  put_str(string("  code $"))
  put_hex(rec_code(recIdx), 2)
  put_str(string(" b23 "))
  put_dec(rec_b23(recIdx))
  put_str(string("  ret $"))
  put_hex(rec_ret(recIdx), 3)
  put_str(string("  C"))
  put_dec((rec_flags(recIdx) >> 1) & 1)
  put_str(string(" Z"))
  put_dec(rec_flags(recIdx) & 1)
  put_str(string("  site "))
  put_str(site_name(siteIdx))
  if siteIdx >= 0
    if site_flags(siteIdx) == FLAGS_ANY
      put_str(string("  flags not judged"))
    elseif rec_flags(recIdx) == site_flags(siteIdx)
      put_str(string("  flags agree"))
    else
      put_str(string("  FLAGS CONTRADICT SITE"))
  put_nl()


PRI check_gates(bDone) | recP
' Gates G1..G5. Each failure prints RIG FAIL and counts.
'
' @param bDone - TRUE when the done flag was set in time

' Local Variables:
' @local recP - record index of a positive control

  if recCount >= 1
    say(string("  G1 at least one record: PASS"))
  else
    say(string("RIG FAIL: G1 no record at all (debug interrupt never entered)"))
    failCount++
  if recCount >= 1
    if rec_b23(0) == 1
      put_str(string("  G2 record 0 b23=1: PASS (its code $"))
      put_hex(rec_code(0), 2)
      put_str(string(" recorded, not judged; return address $"))
      put_hex(rec_ret(0), 3)
      if rec_ret(0) == 0
        say(string(", the first instruction as inferred)"))
      else
        say(string(", NOT the first instruction - informational, no verdict depends on it)"))
    else
      say(string("RIG FAIL: G2 record 0 is not the COGINIT entry (needs b23=1)"))
      failCount++
  recP := siteRec[S_P1]
  if recP >= 0 and rec_code(recP) == $A1 and rec_b23(recP) == 0
    say(string("  G3 p1 record, code $A1, b23=0: PASS"))
  else
    say(string("RIG FAIL: G3 no p1 record with code $A1 and b23=0 (the ISR did not re-arm or return)"))
    failCount++
  recP := siteRec[S_P2]
  if recP >= 0 and rec_code(recP) == $A9 and rec_b23(recP) == 0
    say(string("  G4 p2 record, code $A9, b23=0: PASS"))
  else
    say(string("RIG FAIL: G4 no p2 record with code $A9 and b23=0 (re-arm or return failed partway)"))
    failCount++
  if bDone
    say(string("  G5 done flag within 1 s: PASS"))
  else
    say(string("RIG FAIL: G5 done flag not set within 1 s (records above are whatever existed)"))
    failCount++


PRI print_table_check(tbl, pLabel)
' Print whether the whole record list matches one expected table.
'
' @param tbl - TBL_STUDY, TBL_ABSENT or TBL_OWN
' @param pLabel - line label

  put_str(pLabel)
  if table_matches(tbl)
    say(string("MATCHED"))
  else
    say(string("not matched"))


PRI table_matches(tbl) : bMatch | recIdx, expCode
' TRUE when the records are exactly the table's sites, in order, with its codes.
'
' @param tbl - TBL_STUDY, TBL_ABSENT or TBL_OWN
' @returns bMatch - TRUE on an exact match

' Local Variables:
' @local recIdx - record being compared
' @local expCode - the table's code for that row

  bMatch := recCount == table_len(tbl)
  if bMatch
    repeat recIdx from 0 to recCount - 1
      if recSite[recIdx] <> exp_site(tbl, recIdx)
        bMatch := FALSE
      expCode := exp_code(tbl, recIdx)
      if expCode <> CODE_ANY and rec_code(recIdx) <> expCode
        bMatch := FALSE


PRI site_clean(siteIdx) : bClean
' TRUE when a site has exactly one record and its saved flags agree.
'
' @param siteIdx - site
' @returns bClean - TRUE when usable

  bClean := FALSE
  if siteHits[siteIdx] == 1
    if site_flags(siteIdx) == FLAGS_ANY or rec_flags(siteRec[siteIdx]) == site_flags(siteIdx)
      bClean := TRUE


PRI verdict_break() | entered, flagsBad, dupes
' VERDICT SO109 BREAK: did the condition-false BRKs e1, e2, e3 enter the ISR.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local entered - e-sites with at least one record
' @local flagsBad - entered e-sites whose saved flags contradict the site
' @local dupes - e-sites with more than one record

  entered := 0
  flagsBad := 0
  dupes := 0
  tally_site(S_E1, @entered, @flagsBad, @dupes)
  tally_site(S_E2, @entered, @flagsBad, @dupes)
  tally_site(S_E3, @entered, @flagsBad, @dupes)
  put_str(string("VERDICT SO109 BREAK: "))
  if unattributed > 0
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - records fall outside every site window; the entry point differs from +1/+2"))
  elseif dupes > 0
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - unpredicted: an e-site produced more than one record"))
  elseif flagsBad > 0
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - a saved C/Z contradicts its e-site; that record says nothing about a false condition"))
  elseif entered == 3
    say(string("CONFIRMED - e1, e2 and e3 each entered the debug ISR with their condition false (saved flags agree)"))
    say(string("  as the study predicts, and as v55 :62 and P2 Documentation :2491 both state"))
  elseif entered == 0 and (siteHits[S_T1] == 0 or siteHits[S_T2] == 0)
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - no conditional BRK entered, true ones (t1/t2) included; the rig cannot separate the condition from conditional BRKs not breaking at all"))
  elseif entered == 0
    say(string("REFUTED - no condition-false BRK entered the ISR while t1 and t2 did (this part honours the condition)"))
    say(string("  contradicts the study AND v55 :62 AND P2 Documentation :2491"))
  else
    put_str(string("INCONCLUSIVE - unpredicted: entered at"))
    put_entered(S_E1)
    put_entered(S_E2)
    put_entered(S_E3)
    put_nl()


PRI tally_site(siteIdx, pEntered, pFlagsBad, pDupes)
' Count one e-site into the BREAK tallies.
'
' @param siteIdx - e-site
' @param pEntered - address of the entered tally
' @param pFlagsBad - address of the flags-contradict tally
' @param pDupes - address of the duplicate tally

  if siteHits[siteIdx] > 0
    long[pEntered]++
    if siteHits[siteIdx] > 1
      long[pDupes]++
    elseif rec_flags(siteRec[siteIdx]) <> site_flags(siteIdx)
      long[pFlagsBad]++


PRI put_entered(siteIdx)
' Print " <site>=yes" or " <site>=no".
'
' @param siteIdx - site

  put_str(string(" "))
  put_str(site_name(siteIdx))
  if siteHits[siteIdx] > 0
    put_str(string("=yes"))
  else
    put_str(string("=no"))


PRI verdict_code() | codeE1, codeE2, codeE3
' VERDICT SO109 CODE: STALE (study) / OWN (v55 :62 literal) / OTHER.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local codeE1 - code in the e1 record
' @local codeE2 - code in the e2 record
' @local codeE3 - code in the e3 record

  put_str(string("VERDICT SO109 CODE: "))
  if unattributed > 0
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - records fall outside every site window"))
  elseif not (site_clean(S_E1) and site_clean(S_E2) and site_clean(S_E3))
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - needs one clean record from each of e1, e2, e3 (see VERDICT SO109 BREAK)"))
  elseif not (site_clean(S_T1) and site_clean(S_T2)) or rec_code(siteRec[S_T1]) <> $C3 or rec_code(siteRec[S_T2]) <> $D4
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - true-condition control failed: t1 must show $C3 and t2 $D4, each once, flags agreeing"))
  else
    codeE1 := rec_code(siteRec[S_E1])
    codeE2 := rec_code(siteRec[S_E2])
    codeE3 := rec_code(siteRec[S_E3])
    if codeE1 == $A1 and codeE2 == $D4 and codeE3 == $D4
      say(string("CONFIRMED - STALE: e1/e2/e3 show $A1/$D4/$D4, the last condition-true code"))
      say(string("  bench matched the study and P2 Documentation :2491; NOT v55 :62 read literally (OWN)"))
    elseif codeE1 == $B2 and codeE2 == $E5 and codeE3 == $96
      say(string("REFUTED - OWN: e1/e2/e3 show their own codes $B2/$E5/$96; the code latch ignores the condition too"))
      say(string("  bench matched v55 :62 read literally; NOT the study or P2 Documentation :2491"))
    else
      put_str(string("INCONCLUSIVE - OTHER: e1/e2/e3 show $"))
      put_hex(codeE1, 2)
      put_str(string("/$"))
      put_hex(codeE2, 2)
      put_str(string("/$"))
      put_hex(codeE3, 2)
      say(string(", neither STALE ($A1/$D4/$D4) nor OWN ($B2/$E5/$96)"))


PRI verdict_cancels() | failed
' VERDICT SO109 CANCELS: no record from s1, j1, w1, w3.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local failed - cancel sites that produced a record

  failed := 0
  if siteHits[S_S1] > 0
    failed++
  if siteHits[S_J1] > 0
    failed++
  if siteHits[S_W1] > 0
    failed++
  if siteHits[S_W3] > 0
    failed++
  put_str(string("VERDICT SO109 CANCELS: "))
  if unattributed > 0
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - records fall outside every site window"))
  elseif failed == 0
    say(string("CONFIRMED - no record from s1 (SKIP), j1 (taken JMP), w1 (if_z JMP taken), w3 (if_z SKIP taken)"))
  else
    put_str(string("REFUTED - cancel failed: record at"))
    put_hit(S_S1)
    put_hit(S_J1)
    put_hit(S_W1)
    put_hit(S_W3)
    put_nl()


PRI put_hit(siteIdx)
' Print " <site>" when the site produced a record.
'
' @param siteIdx - site

  if siteHits[siteIdx] > 0
    put_str(string(" "))
    put_str(site_name(siteIdx))


PRI verdict_idioms()
' VERDICT SO109 IDIOMS: w2 (JMP idiom) and w4 (SKIP idiom) deliver $F4 / $F6.
'

  put_str(string("VERDICT SO109 IDIOMS: "))
  if unattributed > 0
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - records fall outside every site window"))
  elseif siteHits[S_W2] == 0 or siteHits[S_W4] == 0
    put_str(string("REFUTED - an idiom suppressed a wanted break: missing"))
    if siteHits[S_W2] == 0
      put_str(string(" w2"))
    if siteHits[S_W4] == 0
      put_str(string(" w4"))
    put_nl()
  elseif siteHits[S_W2] > 1 or siteHits[S_W4] > 1
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - unpredicted: w2 or w4 produced more than one record"))
  elseif not (site_clean(S_W2) and site_clean(S_W4))
    say(string("INCONCLUSIVE - a saved C/Z contradicts w2 or w4"))
  elseif rec_code(siteRec[S_W2]) <> $F4 or rec_code(siteRec[S_W4]) <> $F6
    put_str(string("REFUTED - an idiom delivered the wrong code: w2 $"))
    put_hex(rec_code(siteRec[S_W2]), 2)
    put_str(string(" (want $F4), w4 $"))
    put_hex(rec_code(siteRec[S_W4]), 2)
    say(string(" (want $F6)"))
  else
    say(string("CONFIRMED - w2 (if_z JMP around an unconditional BRK) delivered $F4; w4 (if_z SKIP #1 ahead of it) delivered $F6"))
    say(string("  w3/w4 are the SKIP form v55 :63-64 documents; suppression at w1/w3 is decided by VERDICT SO109 CANCELS"))


' ---- record accessors ----

PRI rec_brk(recIdx) : rawBrk
' @param recIdx - record index
' @returns rawBrk - the raw GETBRK WCZ word

  rawBrk := long[MBOX_REC + recIdx * 8]


PRI rec_iret(recIdx) : rawIret
' @param recIdx - record index
' @returns rawIret - the raw $1FF (IRET0) word

  rawIret := long[MBOX_REC + recIdx * 8 + 4]


PRI rec_code(recIdx) : brkCode
' @param recIdx - record index
' @returns brkCode - GETBRK [31:24]

  brkCode := rec_brk(recIdx) >> 24


PRI rec_b23(recIdx) : entryBit
' @param recIdx - record index
' @returns entryBit - GETBRK bit 23 (1 = COGINIT entry)

  entryBit := (rec_brk(recIdx) >> 23) & 1


PRI rec_ret(recIdx) : retAddr
' @param recIdx - record index
' @returns retAddr - return address, $1FF word [19:0]

  retAddr := rec_iret(recIdx) & RET_MASK


PRI rec_flags(recIdx) : savedFlags
' @param recIdx - record index
' @returns savedFlags - saved (C << 1) | Z from $1FF word bits 31, 30

  savedFlags := (rec_iret(recIdx) >> 30) & %11


' ---- site tables ----

PRI site_brk(siteIdx) : addr
' @param siteIdx - site
' @returns addr - the site's BRK cog address (listing)

  addr := lookupz(siteIdx: BRK_P1, BRK_E1, BRK_T1, BRK_T2, BRK_E2, BRK_E3, BRK_S1, BRK_J1, BRK_W1, BRK_W2, BRK_W3, BRK_W4, BRK_P2)


PRI site_label_addr(siteIdx) : addr
' @param siteIdx - site
' @returns addr - the site's BRK cog address derived from the image labels

  addr := (lookupz(siteIdx: @p1, @e1, @t1, @t2, @e2, @e3, @s1_brk, @j1_brk, @w1_brk, @w2_brk, @w3_brk, @w4_brk, @p2) - @tgt) >> 2


PRI site_kind(siteIdx) : kind
' @param siteIdx - site
' @returns kind - K_POS, K_FALSE, K_TRUE, K_CANCEL or K_IDIOM

  kind := lookupz(siteIdx: K_POS, K_FALSE, K_TRUE, K_TRUE, K_FALSE, K_FALSE, K_CANCEL, K_CANCEL, K_CANCEL, K_IDIOM, K_CANCEL, K_IDIOM, K_POS)


PRI site_flags(siteIdx) : flagRule
' @param siteIdx - site
' @returns flagRule - the (C << 1) | Z the site's BRK sees, or FLAGS_ANY (p1: not judged)

  flagRule := lookupz(siteIdx: FLAGS_ANY, FLAGS_C0Z0, FLAGS_C0Z0, FLAGS_C0Z1, FLAGS_C0Z1, FLAGS_C0Z1, FLAGS_C0Z1, FLAGS_C0Z1, FLAGS_C0Z1, FLAGS_C0Z0, FLAGS_C0Z1, FLAGS_C0Z0, FLAGS_C0Z0)


PRI site_name(siteIdx) : pName
' @param siteIdx - site, S_ENTRY or S_NONE
' @returns pName - printable name (5 characters)

  case siteIdx
    S_ENTRY: pName := string("entry")
    S_P1:    pName := string("p1   ")
    S_E1:    pName := string("e1   ")
    S_T1:    pName := string("t1   ")
    S_T2:    pName := string("t2   ")
    S_E2:    pName := string("e2   ")
    S_E3:    pName := string("e3   ")
    S_S1:    pName := string("s1   ")
    S_J1:    pName := string("j1   ")
    S_W1:    pName := string("w1   ")
    S_W2:    pName := string("w2   ")
    S_W3:    pName := string("w3   ")
    S_W4:    pName := string("w4   ")
    S_P2:    pName := string("p2   ")
    other:   pName := string("NONE ")


' ---- expected-record tables ----

PRI table_len(tbl) : rows
' @param tbl - TBL_STUDY, TBL_ABSENT or TBL_OWN
' @returns rows - records the table expects

  rows := lookupz(tbl: 10, 7, 10)


PRI exp_site(tbl, rowIdx) : siteIdx
' @param tbl - expected table
' @param rowIdx - row
' @returns siteIdx - the site that row expects

  case tbl
    TBL_STUDY, TBL_OWN:
      siteIdx := lookupz(rowIdx: S_ENTRY, S_P1, S_E1, S_T1, S_T2, S_E2, S_E3, S_W2, S_W4, S_P2)
    other:
      siteIdx := lookupz(rowIdx: S_ENTRY, S_P1, S_T1, S_T2, S_W2, S_W4, S_P2)


PRI exp_code(tbl, rowIdx) : brkCode
' @param tbl - expected table
' @param rowIdx - row
' @returns brkCode - the GETBRK code that row expects, or CODE_ANY

  case tbl
    TBL_STUDY:
      brkCode := lookupz(rowIdx: CODE_ANY, $A1, $A1, $C3, $D4, $D4, $D4, $F4, $F6, $A9)
    TBL_OWN:
      brkCode := lookupz(rowIdx: CODE_ANY, $A1, $B2, $C3, $D4, $E5, $96, $F4, $F6, $A9)
    other:
      brkCode := lookupz(rowIdx: CODE_ANY, $A1, $C3, $D4, $F4, $F6, $A9)


' ---- plain serial output on P62 (no DEBUG) ----

PRI put_ch(ch)
' Send one byte and wait until the transmitter is idle.
'
' @param ch - byte to send

  wypin(TX_PIN, ch)
  repeat while rqpin(TX_PIN) & TX_BUSY_BIT


PRI put_str(pStr)
' Send a zero-terminated string.
'
' @param pStr - address of the string

  repeat while byte[pStr]
    put_ch(byte[pStr++])


PRI put_nl()
' End a line (CR LF).
'

  put_ch(13)
  put_ch(10)


PRI say(pStr)
' Send a string and end the line.
'
' @param pStr - address of the string

  put_str(pStr)
  put_nl()


PRI put_hex(value, digits) | nibIdx, nib
' Send value as hex, most significant digit first.
'
' @param value - value to send
' @param digits - number of hex digits (1..8)

' Local Variables:
' @local nibIdx - nibble being sent
' @local nib - its value

  repeat nibIdx from digits - 1 to 0
    nib := (value >> (nibIdx * 4)) & $F
    if nib < 10
      put_ch("0" + nib)
    else
      put_ch("A" + nib - 10)


PRI put_dec(value) | divisor, bStarted
' Send a non-negative value in decimal.
'
' @param value - value to send (0..2_147_483_647)

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - current decimal place
' @local bStarted - TRUE once a non-zero digit has been sent

  divisor := 1_000_000_000
  bStarted := FALSE
  repeat 10
    if value >= divisor or bStarted or divisor == 1
      put_ch("0" + value / divisor)
      value //= divisor
      bStarted := TRUE
    divisor /= 10


PRI put_dec2(value)
' Send 0..99 as two decimal digits.
'
' @param value - value to send

  put_ch("0" + value / 10)
  put_ch("0" + value // 10)


{ DEBUG ISR IMAGE -- 16 longs, assembled at $000, copied by cog 0 to cog 1's
  load area $FFF40. The debug ROM loads it into cog 1's $000..$00F on every
  debug interrupt (after saving the program's $000..$00F) and jumps to $000.
}
DAT             org     0               ' ---- debug ISR image (cog 1, $000..$00F) ----
isr             getbrk  isr_t   wcz     ' [31:24] break code, [23] = COGINIT entry
                mov     isr_r, $1FF     ' IRET0: return address [19:0], C [31], Z [30]
                rdlong  isr_p, isr_b    ' address of the next free record
                wrlong  isr_t, isr_p
                add     isr_p, #4
                wrlong  isr_r, isr_p
                add     isr_p, #4
                wrlong  isr_p, isr_b    ' one 8-byte record per entry
                brk     #$10            ' inside the ISR: arm interrupt-on-BRK (%E) only
                jmp     #\$1FD          ' debug ROM: restore $000..$00F, then RETI0
isr_t           long    0
isr_r           long    0
isr_p           long    0
isr_b           long    MBOX            ' mailbox base
                long    0[2]            ' pad to 16 longs
isr_end

{ TARGET IMAGE -- cog 1, cog exec, assembled at $000. The COGINIT entry lands
  on the first NOP. Every test BRK is followed by two NOPs. Each site's BRK
  line carries its label (sites s1, j1, w1..w4 also label the SKIP/JMP).
}
DAT             org     0               ' ---- target image (cog 1) ----
tgt             nop                     ' COGINIT entry lands here (return $000)
                nop
p1              brk     #$A1            ' positive control: unconditional
                nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #1   wcz ' C=0 Z=0
e1      if_z    brk     #$B2            ' condition FALSE
                nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #1   wcz ' C=0 Z=0
t1      if_nz   brk     #$C3            ' condition true
                nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #0   wcz ' C=0 Z=1
t2      if_z    brk     #$D4            ' condition true
                nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #0   wcz ' C=0 Z=1
e2      if_nz   brk     #$E5            ' condition FALSE
                nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #0   wcz ' C=0 Z=1
e3      if_c    brk     #$96            ' condition FALSE (C flag)
                nop
                nop
s1              skip    #1              ' skip control
s1_brk          brk     #$F1
                nop
                nop
j1              jmp     #j1_land        ' branch control
j1_brk          brk     #$F2
j1_land         nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #0   wcz ' Z=1: the JMP idiom must NOT break
w1      if_z    jmp     #w1_land
w1_brk          brk     #$F3
w1_land         nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #1   wcz ' Z=0: the JMP idiom must break
w2      if_z    jmp     #w2_land
w2_brk          brk     #$F4
w2_land         nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #0   wcz ' Z=1: the SKIP idiom must NOT break
w3      if_z    skip    #1
w3_brk          brk     #$F5
                nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #1   wcz ' Z=0: the SKIP idiom must break
w4      if_z    skip    #1
w4_brk          brk     #$F6
                nop
                nop
p2              brk     #$A9            ' closing positive control
                nop
                nop
                mov     tgt_y, #1
                wrlong  tgt_y, ##MBOX_DONE ' done flag (DONE_VALUE = 1)
                jmp     #$
tgt_y           long    0
tgt_end

